Bundled third-party components
================================================================================

This repository redistributes the following third-party works. Their own licenses
apply to those files and are reproduced alongside them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ThIDE — Therion.Blender, Therion.Build, Therion.Core,
        Therion.Processing.Abstractions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Readers for the compiled cave-survey formats (Therion Loch .lox and Survex .3d),
and the reader for what a Therion compilation printed while it ran. Not vendored:
the source is a Git submodule at server/external/ThIDE, pinned to the commit
below, and the built assemblies are redistributed inside the server image.

  Source:    https://github.com/apgeo/ThIDE
  Commit:    bedfdc71aa972d39b3f6f3f0313c8c7699871534
  License:   MPL-2.0 — see the LICENSE file beside each module under
             server/external/ThIDE/src/

The Mozilla Public License is file-level copyleft, and these sources are
deliberately not marked "Incompatible With Secondary Licenses", so they combine
into this work's AGPL-3.0-or-later terms under MPL-2.0 section 3.3. Modifications
to the MPL-covered files are published in the repository named above.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CaveView.js
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A 3D cave-survey viewer, vendored as a prebuilt runtime bundle under
client/public/caveview/. Used on demand by the embedded 3D viewer.

  Source:    https://github.com/aardgoose/CaveView.js (release 2.9.0)
  License:   MIT — see client/public/caveview/LICENSE
  Provenance: client/public/caveview/README.md

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
karstnet reference networks
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two published example karst networks (the Huttes and Sakany .dat files under
server/tests/SilexGis.Api.Tests/Fixtures/Karstnet/), redistributed unmodified as
test fixtures. The topology metrics computed for them are committed beside them so
the test suite can assert against the reference arithmetic without the reference
implementation installed. Test fixtures only: nothing here is built into a shipped
artifact.

  Source:    https://github.com/karstnet/karstnet (data/)
  License:   MIT (c) 2018-2024 Philippe Renard, Pauline Collon
  Full text: server/tests/SilexGis.Api.Tests/Fixtures/Karstnet/NOTICE.md

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Feature symbol icons
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The 19 PNG symbols under client/public/feature_symbols/ (used to render surface
features on the map). These originate from earlier SilexGIS versions.

  Provenance and license status: client/public/feature_symbols/PROVENANCE.md

================================================================================
Dependencies
================================================================================

SilexGIS is built with open-source libraries obtained through NuGet (server) and
npm (client); those are not redistributed here as source. Their licenses are those
declared by each package. Notable runtime components include ASP.NET Core,
OpenIddict, EF Core with Npgsql and NetTopologySuite, GDAL (via MaxRev.Gdal),
React, Ant Design and OpenLayers.
